The idea is that by letting handlers accept this wrapper, the wrapper function can have more complicated logic inside that allows to provide this value for any kind of underlying representation, be it listpack, string map or even an offloaded value (#5896 will be integrated here as well)

```c++
 auto cb = [field = args[1]](const HMapWrap& hw) -> OpResult<string> {
  if (auto it = hw.Find(field); it)
    return string{it->second};
  return OpStatus::KEY_NOTFOUND;
};
OpResult<string> result = cmd_cntx.tx->ScheduleSingleHopT(WrapRO(cb));
```
